            <div xml:id="d198">

                <pb facs="0349" n="235" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg235"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/5001: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Yugoslavia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Prince</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Belgrade</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-08-24T10:00:00+01:00">August 24, 1931—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:20 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>40. Yugoslav Government disturbed over semi-official news from Washington to
                    effect Hoover Plan will be applied Yugoslavia despite non-acceptance. Finance
                    Ministry operating radical budget cuts every Ministry but states cannot possibly
                    meet Hoover requirements in addition present abnormal burdens incident to recent
                    currency stabilization and deficit incurred through aid guaranteed grain <pb
                        facs="0350" n="236" xml:id="pg236"/> farmers. Finance Minister expresses
                    belief, hope Yugoslavia will receive aid this crisis essential to preservation
                    currency and credit.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Prince</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
